1082
00:47:57,910 --> 00:48:00,040
we would not observe
the model's ability

1083
00:48:00,040 --> 00:48:01,690
to generalize to test data.

1084
00:48:01,690 --> 00:48:03,460
We don't observe this.

1085
00:48:03,460 --> 00:48:05,810
So obviously, it
seems like this kind

1086
00:48:05,810 --> 00:48:09,040
of blocking of back
propagation on labels

1087
00:48:09,040 --> 00:48:13,330
that are visible at input
to the NPT is helping.

1088
00:48:13,330 --> 00:48:16,630
It could also be possible
that in BERT style

1089
00:48:16,630 --> 00:48:18,820
stochastic masking,
you also randomly will

1090
00:48:18,820 --> 00:48:23,260
flip some labels to be
in a different category.

1091
00:48:23,260 --> 00:48:25,240
So this is kind of
just like a random fine

1092
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:28,510
print that was introduced
in the BERT masking text.

1093
00:48:28,510 --> 00:48:29,360
We also do that.

1094
00:48:29,360 --> 00:48:32,800
So it's possible that
somehow contributes to that.

1095
00:48:32,800 --> 00:48:35,873
But it's probably pretty
likely to just be the fact

1096
00:48:35,873 --> 00:48:38,290
that we're not back propagating
a loss on something that's

1097
00:48:38,290 --> 00:48:39,870
visible.

1098
00:48:39,870 --> 00:48:40,370
Great.

